speechtext:
Mr. Speaker, there have been discussions among the various representatives in the House and I believe you will find unanimous consent for the following motion:
That notwithstanding any Standing Orders and usual practices of this House, the House withdraw Government Motion No. 4 after the adoption of this order and that;
After the return to work of the employees of the Public Service Alliance of Canada and other related unions, proceeding on Bill C-29, an act respecting compensation in the public sector of Canada and to amend another act in relation thereto, be halted immediately after second reading and not proceeded further with;
Should the PSAC and Treasury Board fail to reach an agreement with ensuing public inconvenience, then Bill C-29, an act respecting compensation in the public sector of Canada and to amend another act in relation thereto, would be deemed referred to a Committee of the Whole House; and that, immediately at the beginning of Government Orders the House shall begin its study at Committee of the Whole of the said bill and that all questions to dispose of the said bill at that stage and report stage be put without further debate or amendment no later than 10 p.m. that day.
That the following sitting day, the House shall begin consideration at third reading to Bill C-29, and that all questions to dispose of the said bill at that stage be put without further debate or amendment no later than 10 p.m. that day.
Mr. Speaker, I should also indicate that I believe you will find unanimous consent to complete the second reading of Bill C-29 now without further debate. I might add that the vote would be deemed demanded and deferred until tomorrow at three o'clock p.m.
